<blockquote class="uncited"><div>The CPS is compiled for X86 however it is dependany on Dot Net 4.8, and I don't know if that version of Dot Net is available for W7 32 bit<br><br>Why don't you simply install a newer version of Windows e.g. Windows 10 IOT</div></blockquote>I’ve been programming Motorola radios for decades. They need to use a laptop from the same era they were made. For my System Sabers, I  have a true DOS Toshiba Satellite. For my MTS2000’s, &amp; other radios from the 90’s, I have a Windows XP laptop. For my XTS’s, XTL’s, &amp; Trbo radios, I use my Windows 7 32 bit laptop, &amp; for my newest APX’s, I do use a Windows 10 laptop. So if I need Windows 10, I have a laptop for that, but I’d rather use my Windows 7 laptop if I could. So I’d rather know which laptop I could use. But  I’d prefer the 7 laptop because it’s much smaller, &amp; easier to carry around. GARY<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8235">N4KVE</a> — Tue Mar 11, 2025 9:04 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
